meta {
  name: Account Storage
  type: http
  seq: 50
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/v1/accounts/{{did}}/storage
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{adminToken}}
}

docs {
  # GET /v1/accounts/:id/storage

  Operator blob-storage metrics for an account, for the provisioning dashboard.
  `:id` is the account DID. Reports on the account regardless of activation
  state. Admin-authed: the master token (shown here) **or** an active operator
  companion-app device's signed request.

  Response (camelCase, matching the rest of the /v1 API):
  - `blobCount` — number of blobs stored for the account.
  - `totalBytes` — total bytes occupied by those blobs.
  - `uploadedBlobCount` / `uploadedBlobBytes` — physical blob rows recording this
    account as their *uploader*, and their bytes. A second witness beside the two
    figures above: those come from `blob_owners`, as does every other blob surface
    an operator can reach, so ownership rows vanishing and bytes being destroyed
    look identical everywhere else. These read the physical table directly.

    Blobs are shared, so a gap in either direction is benign on its own — a CID this
    account references but another uploaded, or one it uploaded that only another
    account still owns. Treat it as a prompt to look, not a verdict.

    Read the pair together against `blobCount`:
    - `blobCount = 0`, `uploadedBlobCount > 0` — the bytes are on disk and the
      account's **ownership rows** are what went missing.
    - `blobCount = 0`, `uploadedBlobCount = 0` — the **bytes themselves** are gone.

    Note the second case: a physical row is deleted with its last owner, taking its
    uploader attribution with it, so this witness reaches zero too when GC is what
    destroyed the blobs. `uploadedBlobCount = 0` means "nothing is left", **not**
    "nothing was ever here".
  - `quotaBytes` — the per-account storage quota (`[blobs] max_storage_per_account`).
    Tiers are not yet differentiated in v0.1, so every account reports the same
    configured quota.
  - `quotaUsedPct` — `totalBytes` as a percentage of `quotaBytes` (0 when the
    quota is 0).
  - `largestBlob` — the account's largest blob as `{ cid, size }`, or `null`
    when it has none.

  An unknown DID returns 404.
}
